WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.084
There's only two ways to

00:00:01.084 --> 00:00:02.419
get out of the Gaza Strip.

00:00:02.419 --> 00:00:03.712
There's the north border crossing,

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:04.754
which goes into Israel.

00:00:04.754 --> 00:00:06.256
And then there's the southern crossing

00:00:06.256 --> 00:00:07.382
that goes into Egypt.

00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:08.717
Since Hamas's attacks,

00:00:08.717 --> 00:00:09.676
Israel has closed

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.677
this northern border,

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.095
leaving the crossing with Egypt

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:13.430
as the only way out.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:14.472
But Egypt doesn't

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:16.433
want to let Palestinians in.

00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:17.934
The country is not interested

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:20.812
in housing a bunch of refugees from Gaza.

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:21.688
And they're worried that

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.356
because Israel is planning

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.899
to invade the Gaza Strip,

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:26.317
if these Palestinians come in,

00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:27.402
they may never go home.

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:29.154
So, Palestinians are effectively trapped

00:00:29.154 --> 00:00:30.697
in this small rectangle

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:31.281
that is turning more

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:32.574
and more into a war zone.

00:00:32.574 --> 00:00:33.450
Joe Biden swooped in

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.659
and made a deal with Egypt

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:35.910
to let humanitarian

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.537
aid come in through the southern border.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:38.788
But there's still no news on

00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:39.205
whether or not

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.915
the Palestinians will be able to leave.

00:00:40.915 --> 00:00:42.375
And that is a big question for these

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.877
2 million people living in Gaza.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:44.794
If you want to better understand

00:00:44.794 --> 00:00:46.629
global politics, follow along for more.

